  "numbering_convention": "Board oriented as in the 2026-08-01 photo: silkscreen title readable top-left, 'Logic board'/J2 at LEFT, 'Display'/J3 at RIGHT, probe header vertical in middle. FLEX pin N == probe-header pin N == net /(N+1), for N = 1..34. Header pin 1 is TOP-LEFT; odd pins are the LEFT column, even pins the RIGHT column; numbering increases downward, two pins per row, 17 rows. FLEX pin 1 is the TOPMOST live conductor. The 35th (topmost) connector position is unused on both FPC connectors (J2 pad 1, J3 pad 35) and is not part of this numbering. This is an internal convention anchored to physical geometry; it is NOT claimed to match Apple's own pin-1 designation.",
